{"c":[{"id":"bcd860fe20ff53b5","sum":"C1-J1, H11-H13: page plans end in a hand-off row; host.sock is in <home>/sockets; Jev has a daily cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP); inject test pageFields over the debug socket; page offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; never lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"37e4af8adcf8abcf","sum":"C1-H12: WARNS-word sentences go whole; page plans end with a row:true hand-off; Asks read the tab left only at fill/pagePlan; host.sock in <home>/sockets (CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full); .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wraps; no lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd14b8843dd9d3ee","sum":"C1-I6: a WARNS-word sentence goes whole or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off (no executor step); an Ask reads the tab left only at its fill step or pagePlan; ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone; the hourly budget holds pageWalked.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2691af9702ea9f68","sum":"C1-I6: a value whose sentence holds a WARNS word goes with it as a required clause or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off step ('You press <label>' / 'The rest is yours') with no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-df47ef2e50ca5a79","text":"C1: a value whose own sentence holds a WARNS word goes with that sentence as a required clause or not at all; sentence ends are conservative (lowercase word or digit before, capital after). Whole-line clauses cost corpus clinic-intake two values.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062218Z-bb39f9f0467bc5ce","text":"I6: page plans end with a GoalStep row:true (kind handoff, 'You press <label>' or 'The rest is yours'); it is always the last step, lower.ts gives it no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter than seg.steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"740e3d49bc3a2762","sum":"I6: an Ask reads the tab left only at planAsk's fill step or pagePlan (owner: offer key or goal id); ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone (goalOnPage); the hourly budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T062227Z-47ccc650cd567ff8","text":"I6: an Ask's tab read happens only at planAsk's fill step (fillModel) or in pagePlan; owners are the offer key or goal id; ambient fill/ready-on-load leave a page with a planning/awaiting/running goal alone (goalOnPage) and TabSource refuses an ambient read over a pinned goal.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-6c026cce4f5fd842","text":"I6: page-loop-eval runs every page in one helper; the hourly offer budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked before the ready-on-load check, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour; fill.load_held_<rule> counts holds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c154314373edc26c","sum":"H11-H12: host.sock in <home>/sockets, release answers state+spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; route page-engine test apply to its own helper; .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wrapped panels (exact width); never lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e0b1d7fe48d167f","sum":"H12-I6: host.sock is <home>/sockets/host.sock; release builds answer only state and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (harnesses setenv it); onboarding auto only without --home/--settings; helper page-engine tests route apply to their own helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T035452Z-68fb99dd307065d5","text":"H12: host.sock moved to <home>/sockets/host.sock (default CaretV2/sockets); release builds answer only state (allowlist) and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full, so release-build harnesses must setenv it. Onboarding defaults to auto only without --home/--settings.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-7e02cffa1979776c","text":"I6: helper tests with a page engine must route its apply to their own helper (capture it in a local); a shared 'helper' variable lets an earlier test's trailing walk land in the next test's model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86a6db3d2adf8e6a","sum":"H11: under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) wrapped text measures as one line and panels clip: use an exact .frame(width:) with vertical fixedSize; build.lock is a symlink to heavy.lock, so lockf build.lock inside with-heavy deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T063851Z-1e89e23b19f1384e","text":"H11: a SwiftUI view under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) is measured at its ideal width, so wrapped text counts as one line and the panel clips its top and bottom; give it an exact .frame(width:) and fixedSize(vertical) only (PopupView PopupWidth).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T063851Z-3a51e09ec56311ba","text":"H11: ~/.caret-run/locks/build.lock is a symlink to ~/.long-run/locks/heavy.lock; wrapping lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.sh (which holds heavy.lock) deadlocks while holding the heavy lease.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1ef09e53bf12acfa","sum":"J1-H13: Jev confidence (p_max-1/n)/(1-1/n); daily cap throws JevCapError; replay cache fixture-only; no distilling Jev output; test pageFields via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page; launchd argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d174639a9c85f705","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n); a daily spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP $0.50) throws JevCapError; the replay cache takes fixture text only; TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"987e4b1534648136","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (not the top-two margin judge.ts says; equal only for n=2); makeJevClient holds a per-day spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50) and throws JevCapError; vitest uses a temp spend dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065440Z-6320f5713756d4a4","text":"J1: TypeSafe documents Jev's Choice confidence as (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (docs.typesafe.ai/confidence), not the top-two margin routing/judge.ts describes; the two agree only for two options. engines/decide/confidence.ts computes other engines' confidence this way.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065544Z-2b923d2a58b8f2cf","text":"J1: makeJevClient holds every request against a per-day spend file (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50; CARET_JEV_SPEND_DIR) and throws JevCapError (kind cap) past it; vitest.config.ts points the spend dir at a temp dir.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0d659675b89b1bba","sum":"J1: the replay cache and --log-requests take only fixture text (harness lists fixture window ids; the helper refuses the cache); TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output: train local models on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065553Z-29f2d5c421092ef7","text":"J1: the replay cache (engines/decide/cache.ts) and --log-requests take only fixture text: a harness lists its fixture window ids and says if its memory and plan text (window id 'plan') are fixtures; charged windows are checked too. The helper refuses CARET_JEV_CACHE.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065553Z-310f47ee41817c11","text":"J1: TypeSafe's Master Customer Agreement s2.3(b) (2026-09-23) forbids using Jev's Output for distillation or to train an imitating model; train a local model on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e39825f89d0ff0d","sum":"H12-H13: inject a test pageField via the host debug socket (the bundled helper gets allowlisted env only); page inline offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; a note window needs its own app in helper tests; launchd's argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"379ec0af76ae5f62","sum":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher), so inject a test pageField via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page (native ghost clears skip them), insertsText false, and Tab sends pageInsert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-2110f7480275cbcf","text":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher: HOME, USER, LANG, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, CARET_ENV_FILE...), so a helper-side test switch never reaches it from Caret.app; inject a pageField through the host debug socket instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T080508Z-bc4a09143ef1ff5b","text":"H13: page inline offers use OfferSource.page (never .engine), so HostCoordinator's ghost clears on AX focus changes leave them alone; Claim.insertsText is false for a page ghost and PageInlineMachine sends pageInsert.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"940d166167db3d8d","sum":"H12-H13: launchd starts the agent with relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret' (use launchctl print's pid or lsof); in helper tests a non-page window with the browser's pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar, so give a note window its own app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-ed6af011d8df3dcf","text":"H13: in helper tests, a non-page window sharing the page's browser pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar (H10 ScreenModel.windowBefore); give a note window its own app (NOTES_APP) or TabSource reads the wrong tab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T082217Z-6e9f887494c1affe","text":"H12: launchd starts the SMAppService agent as relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret', so pgrep/ps matching on /Applications/Caret.app misses the host; use launchctl print's pid or lsof txt. A fresh VM guest makes no helper Jev request (no transfers), fill or first look.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"11ec014c3ef4eda5","sum":"C2-GW1 fill+Laya lore: memoryRefOf for refs; >20-field forms split in parts; joined fills keep caller identity; gateway.only = provider; Laya fixture-only, 422s >512 tokens, 5 req/min (no Ask; slow-eval.sh, laya.lock). with-heavy: free disk - --est-disk >= 8 GiB. closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9061cdc44b6fa399","sum":"C2/F2/GW1 fill lore: memory refs via memoryRefOf; forms over 20 fields split into parts accepted and undone alone; joined ambient fills promoted to explicit, keeping caller identity; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9663e92a97e02b87","sum":"C2 fill lore: build Step.memory refs with memoryRefOf, never by hand; countries come only from closed state/province lists; forms over 20 fields split into parts of <=20, each accepted and undone alone; page-loop-eval retries Fill all after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cc84b3cf81253ebf","sum":"C2: build Step.memory refs (id[#part][~option|~date]) with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand; placeWithCountry adds a country only from the closed US-state/CA-province lists, for fields asksPlace accepts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-15cdbeee47a325f7","text":"C2: Step.memory refs are id[#part][~option|~date]; memoryWrites checks text exactly and only options/dates through their conversion. Build refs with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085433Z-9b6840ae7771fd2d","text":"C2: placeWithCountry adds a country only by the closed US-state/CA-province lists and only for fields asksPlace accepts; the engine still needs exactly one loaded option equal to it. About country is deliberately not used.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d359c1b9ca63551e","sum":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (reason moreFields), each run and undone on its own goalAccept; page-loop-eval's Fill all can race the page's ready-on-load fill, so it asks again after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-a637346e142ef258","text":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (page-planner parts, lower.ts cut, reason moreFields); each part runs only on its own goalAccept and undoes as task goal:sN. Fields past 4 parts are named as the user's.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085434Z-d647567d5018f182","text":"C2: page-loop-eval's corpus Fill all can race the page's own ready-on-load fill (helper.fill returns null for a form in flight, no error); the row now asks again after 500 ms and logs it.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8c7e4d7077b1a19","sum":"F2/GW1 fill and gateway lore: joined ambient fills are promoted to explicit; fill joins keep the caller's identity across waits; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bbf67222105d2e73","sum":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publishing, since ambient pop-ups fill no proposals. GW1: providerOptions.gateway.only names the serving provider from the model's endpoints API (laya-free is served by boundless).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T092359Z-18f5690369a8fa9a","text":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publication: ambient pop-ups do not populate proposals, so returning their FillProposal alone cannot serve handleFillAll. Different field scopes in one window wait and resolve fields again.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T094129Z-8c5d1007dd7df018","text":"GW1: the gateway serves convaiinnovations/laya-free through boundless, not convaiinnovations; providerOptions.gateway.only must use the serving provider listed by the model's endpoints API.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"79e694bb1404294d","sum":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training): harnessEngine fixture provenance only, shipped apps refuse it. Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor and keep the caller's reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T100225Z-f4d02db1f4186bed","text":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only because its boundless endpoint permits training; use harnessEngine fixture provenance even with cache off. Generic clients without fixture provenance refuse it, and shipped-app markers always refuse it. Gateway Jev keeps normal sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102153Z-a32a254ad92c6952","text":"Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor: capped formFields can match scopes with different ranked controls. Preserve the caller reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3364d678b58484b","sum":"Free Laya 422s >512 tokens, JSON state, long options; 5 req/min: no Ask there (slow-eval.sh, laya.lock). Fill joins: one trigger, ordered inputs. with-heavy: free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB; host build 3/2. Keep one of duplicate naps. Chrome insertText undo: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97ddef9eec5e365c","sum":"A1/R1 Laya lore: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 tokens, JSON-object state and long choice options, and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (scope-reading.ts); run Laya evals via slow-eval.sh under laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b49778a23660a963","sum":"A1: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 input tokens and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts), the heads 'reading' question confirms it, and ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102251Z-3a116bbdf83faf20","text":"A1: free Laya (gateway, boundless) 422s any request over ~512 input tokens (489 ok, ~519 not) and allows 5 req/min per team; heads and corpus fill requests are ~2000 tokens, so the Ask path cannot run on Laya as built (evidence/screen/a1/laya-limits.txt).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102251Z-6d4e95952b64681c","text":"A1: Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts; any unread word means no reading); the heads 'reading' question confirms it and intent.agreed skips confirmScope/sectionScope. ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bb813feffb3f3c1","sum":"R1: free Laya 422s JSON-object state and choice options over ~300 chars, so Ask-led evals there mostly fail; helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs eval sets on Laya in the background (a 429 ends the pass); queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102855Z-241459cd7cad2754","text":"R1: free Laya gives HTTP 422 for a JSON-object state (harness.ts layaState sends JSON text) and for a choice question whose options total over ~300 chars (heads' scope: 634), so Ask-led evals on Laya are mostly rejected (evidence/screen/r1/probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102855Z-7e60ee41200b62c5","text":"R1: helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs all eval sets on Laya in the background; a 429 ends the pass and the set reruns from the replay cache. Other Laya users queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock; rejected requests replay from cache/failures.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"74a3e62ead206367","sum":"Fill joins need one trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. with-heavy needs free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB (swap counts): ask 3 mem/2 disk for a host build. Merged v2/* may hold a note in two naps; keep one. Chrome joins insertText to the typing undo step: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8208911c044286ba","sum":"Fill joins need the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB (swap growth counts), so ask the smallest honest estimate (a host build: 3 mem / 2 disk).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T114711Z-5f2b276e7a41de4a","text":"Fill joins require the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs: descriptor admission can omit different fields even when input sets match. Different triggers wait with their own captured identity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T132506Z-afeea7cd00f9f436","text":"H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus your --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB, so at about 10 GiB free a 2 GiB build waits; ask for the smallest honest estimate (harness build 3 mem / 2 disk), and swap growth on this Mac eats the same disk.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2aa517edf32bae42","sum":"I7: merged v2/* can hold one note in naps on both sides; keep one nap. a1-ask-reading once lost names at load ~11. Chrome joins insertText to the open typing undo step (one Cmd-Z took typed text too); setting the caret by script first closes it (insert.ts closeTyping).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T133620Z-cd21a7d05fec9102","text":"I7: merged v2/* branches can hold the same notes in naps on both sides (clean git merge, wake shows them twice); find leaves in two .tree files, keep one nap. a1-ask-reading 'acts on code's reading' lost names once in a default-worker suite at load ~11.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T161827Z-f17cd09096e8e827","text":"Chrome joins execCommand('insertText') to the open typing undo step, so one Cmd-Z also removed typed text in a contenteditable. Setting the caret by script where it already is closes the step: extension/src/content/insert.ts closeTyping.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
